      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T06:30:06Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(thread): a matched thread mill verifies clean - the gouge laws read its major circle\n\nA Thread op's helix runs the thread depth (0.5413 x pitch) past the\ndeclared hole, which is the thread's minor circle, by design. Every\nmatched thread mill was blocked, model- and stock-sourced alike:\n\n- law (b) read the declared rim at the minor circle: the Thread arm now\n  moves each hole's rim out to the major circle\n  (material_source::major_rims);\n- the containment solid law read the model's minor wall: a hit is now\n  excused only on the thread's own material (the minor wall, or the face\n  the hole opens through) while the swept cutter stays inside the major\n  cylinder (sim::verify::thread_bore, solid_hits_threaded). Floors, other\n  walls and cuts past the major circle still convict;\n- the crossing law read the retract (the ride reversed at feed) as a\n  crossing pair per turn: chords that only touch, an endpoint within 1 nm\n  of the other's line, are no crossing. proper_cross excused a touch only\n  at an exactly zero orientation, and the reversed arcs' joints stand a\n  last bit off.\n\nPinned by thread_mill_rim (matched clean in air, in a drilled hole and\nfrom the stock; convicts past a wall, wider than the model's hole and\nbelow its floor) and crossing_retrace (a retraced helix is no crossing;\na real crossing still is, down to 0.001 rad).\n\nFixes #1071\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
